-- title:
--   Determinant-one elements act trivially modulo a unipotent-trivial subspace
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, so that $F = \mathbb{Q}_{(p)}$ denotes the $p$-adic completion, and let $\theta = (\theta_0,\theta_1)$ be a pair of monoid homomorphisms $F^\times \to \mathbb{C}^\times$. Write $I(\theta)$ for the space `principalSeries2 p θ`: the $\mathbb{C}$-subspace of functions $f : \mathrm{GL}_2(F) \to \mathbb{C}$ that are locally constant, satisfy $f(n(x)g) = f(g)$ for all $x \in F$ and $g$, where $n(x) = \begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, and satisfy $f(\mathrm{diag}(a_0,a_1)g) = \theta_0(a_0)\theta_1(a_1)\,\sqrt{\|a_0\|/\|a_1\|}\,f(g)$ for all $a_0,a_1 \in F^\times$ and $g$; let $\rho =$ `principalSeries2Rep θ` be the associated right-translation action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ on $I(\theta)$, $(\rho(g)f)(h) = f(hg)$. Let $V \subseteq I(\theta)$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-subspace such that $\rho(g)v \in V$ for every $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ and every $v \in V$, and such that $\rho(n(x))f - f \in V$ for every $x \in F$ and every $f \in I(\theta)$. Then for every $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ with $\det g = 1$ and every $f \in I(\theta)$ one has $\rho(g)f - f \in V$.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic step in the standard irreducibility analysis of a normalised principal series of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$: the elements acting trivially on the quotient by an invariant subspace form a normal subgroup, and $\mathrm{SL}_2$ of a field is generated by elementary unipotent matrices. It is used by [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.eq_top_of_stable_of_forall_principalSeries2Rep_upperUnipotent2_sub_mem_of_norm_eq_one`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.eq_top_of_stable_of_forall_principalSeries2Rep_upperUnipotent2_sub_mem_of_norm_eq_one) to conclude that such a subspace is everything.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_principalSeries2Rep_sub_mem_of_det_eq_one_of_forall_upperUnipotent2_sub_mem.lean

